Ice Ball deals damage for 5 turns, doubling in power each turn. The move stops if it misses on any turn. If it doesn''t miss, Ice Ball will deal 30, 60, 120, 240 and 480 base power damage each turn respectively.
If the user has used Defense Curl in any previous turn (without switching out) then Ice Ball doubles in power, i.e. it will deal 60, 120, 240, 480 and 960 base power damage respectively.
As Ice Ball has 90% accuracy, the chances of it being successful for each turn (with normal Accuracy/Evasion and no other interruptions) are 90%, 81%, 73%, 66% and 59% respectively. In other words, roughly 3 out of every 5 times Ice Ball is used, it will hit for the full 5 turns.
When a Pokémon is holding Icium Z and uses its Z-Power, Ice Ball turns into Subzero Slammer and has base power 100.
Targets a single adjacent Pokémon.
These Pokémon learn Ice Ball at the level specified. The numbers given are for
Pokémon Ultra Sun & Ultra Moon and may vary in other games; check the respective Pokédex pages for details.
These Pokémon can learn Ice Ball as an egg move.
Their breeding groups are also shown for reference.', 'Ice Ball inflige daño durante 5 turnos, duplicando su poder en cada turno. El movimiento se detiene si falla en cualquier turno. Si no falla, Ice Ball infligirá 30, 60, 120, 240 y 480 de daño de potencia base en cada turno, respectivamente.
Si el usuario ha usado Defense Curl en cualquier turno anterior (sin cambiar), entonces Ice Ball duplica su poder, es decir, infligirá 60, 120, 240, 480 y 960 de daño de poder base respectivamente.
Como Ice Ball tiene un 90 % de precisión, las posibilidades de que tenga éxito en cada turno (con precisión/evasión normal y sin otras interrupciones) son del 90 %, 81 %, 73 %, 66 % y 59 %, respectivamente. En otras palabras, aproximadamente 3 de cada 5 veces que se usa Ice Ball, golpeará durante los 5 turnos completos.
Cuando un Pokémon sostiene Icium Z y usa su Z-Power, Ice Ball se convierte en Subzero Slammer y tiene un poder base de 100.
Apunta a un único Pokémon adyacente.
