In the wild, Roar causes the target Pokémon to flee if they are of a lower level, and the battle ends.
In trainer battles (including linked battles), Roar forces the target to switch out of battle (regardless of level) and is replaced with another Pokémon in the trainer''s team.
Pokémon with the abilities Soundproof or Suction Cups or those rooted by Ingrain are not affected by Roar.
When a Pokémon is holding Normalium Z and uses its Z-Power, Roar turns into Z-Roar and raises Defense one stage, in addition to its usual effect as above.
Targets a single adjacent Pokémon.
These Pokémon learn Roar at the level specified. The numbers given are for
Pokémon Sword & Shield and may vary in other games; check the respective Pokédex pages for details.
These Pokémon can learn Roar as an egg move.
Their breeding groups are also shown for reference.', 'En la naturaleza, Roar hace que el Pokémon objetivo huya si es de un nivel inferior y la batalla termina.
En las batallas de entrenador (incluidas las batallas vinculadas), Roar obliga al objetivo a salir de la batalla (sin importar el nivel) y es reemplazado por otro Pokémon en el equipo del entrenador.
Los Pokémon con las habilidades Soundproof o Suction Cups o aquellos rooteados por Ingrain no se ven afectados por Roar.
Cuando un Pokémon sostiene Normalium Z y usa su Z-Power, Roar se convierte en Z-Roar y aumenta la Defensa un nivel, además de su efecto habitual como se indicó anteriormente.
Apunta a un único Pokémon adyacente.
