Rollout deals damage for 5 turns, doubling in power each turn. The move stops if it misses on any turn. If it doesn''t miss, Rollout will deal 30, 60, 120, 240 and 480 base power damage each turn respectively.
If the user has used Defense Curl in any previous turn (without switching out) then Rollout doubles in power, i.e. it will deal 60, 120, 240, 480 and 960 base power damage respectively.
As Rollout has 90% accuracy, the chances of it being successful for each turn (with normal Accuracy/Evasion and no other interruptions) are 90%, 81%, 73%, 66% and 59% respectively. In other words, roughly 3 out of every 5 times Rollout is used, it will hit for the full 5 turns.
When a Pokémon is holding Rockium Z and uses its Z-Power, Rollout turns into Continental Crush and has base power 100.
Targets a single adjacent Pokémon.
These Pokémon learn Rollout at the level specified. The numbers given are for
Pokémon Sword & Shield and may vary in other games; check the respective Pokédex pages for details.
These Pokémon can learn Rollout as an egg move.
Their breeding groups are also shown for reference.', 'Rollout inflige daño durante 5 turnos, duplicando su poder cada turno. El movimiento se detiene si falla en cualquier turno. Si no falla, Rollout infligirá 30, 60, 120, 240 y 480 de daño de potencia base en cada turno, respectivamente.
Si el usuario ha usado Defense Curl en cualquier turno anterior (sin cambiar), entonces Rollout duplica su poder, es decir, infligirá 60, 120, 240, 480 y 960 de daño de poder base respectivamente.
Como Rollout tiene un 90 % de precisión, las posibilidades de que tenga éxito en cada turno (con Precisión/Evasión normal y sin otras interrupciones) son del 90 %, 81 %, 73 %, 66 % y 59 %, respectivamente. En otras palabras, aproximadamente 3 de cada 5 veces que se usa Rollout, golpeará durante los 5 turnos completos.
Cuando un Pokémon sostiene Rockium Z y usa su Z-Power, Rollout se convierte en Continental Crush y tiene un poder base de 100.
Apunta a un único Pokémon adyacente.
